{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FEkCr6TxFJSLbhqpXdMjkh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 635,\n3\t  \"title\": \"[REQUEST] Option to render a Table without the header row\",\n4\t  \"body\": \"NOTE: If a feature could be implemented in a third-party library, then it is unlikely to be accepted as part of the core library.\\n\\nNOTE: Feature requests will not be considered unless first approved in discussions (https://github.com/textualize/rich/discussions)\\n\\nHave you checked the issues for a similar suggestions?\\n\\n**How would you improve Rich?**\\n\\nI print several small tables to the terminal as a status report, and the column names are obvious from the data. The header row takes up a line and a separator on every table, which adds up when there are ten of them.\\n\\nPlease add a way to render a `Table` with just the data rows and no header row at all.\\n\\n**What problem does it solve for you?**\\n\\nMy status output would fit on one screen. At the moment I strip the first lines from the captured output, which breaks when a cell wraps.\",\n5\t  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n6\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-29T15:00:00Z\",\n7\t  \"labels\": [\n8\t    \"Needs triage\"\n9\t  ]\n10\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4d81f5a-64c7-4f53-97e6-9b81327d2d47","uuid":"098dde43-cd65-4db3-a0b4-8317f422aef5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:19:59.846Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"number\": 635,\n  \"title\": \"[REQUEST] Option to render a Table without the header row\",\n  \"body\": \"NOTE: If a feature could be implemented in a third-party library, then it is unlikely to be accepted as part of the core library.\\n\\nNOTE: Feature requests will not be considered unless first approved in discussions (https://github.com/textualize/rich/discussions)\\n\\nHave you checked the issues for a similar suggestions?\\n\\n**How would you improve Rich?**\\n\\nI print several small tables to the terminal as a status report, and the column names are obvious from the data. The header row takes up a line and a separator on every table, which adds up when there are ten of them.\\n\\nPlease add a way to render a `Table` with just the data rows and no header row at all.\\n\\n**What problem does it solve for you?**\\n\\nMy status output would fit on one screen. At the moment I strip the first lines from the captured output, which breaks when a cell wraps.\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-29T15:00:00Z\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"Needs triage\"\n  ]\n}","numLines":10,"startLine":1,"totalLines":10}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FEkCr6TxFJSLbhqpXdMjkh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
